    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 261 tests pass. Here's what I did to consolidate duplicate detection into a single `identityKey`.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Single derived key on the entity** \u2014 `Owner.getIdentityKey()` (`model/Owner.java`, `@Transient`) returns `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`.\n\n**One consolidated check** \u2014 new `EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique` step compares the new owner's whole `identityKey` against every existing owner's, throwing the new checked `DuplicateIdentityException` (\u2192 409 via `DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML) only on an exact full-key match.\n\n**Pipeline rewiring** (`owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 removed the three separate steps (`ensureTelephoneUnique` \u2192 `ensureEmailUnique` \u2192 `ensureHouseholdUnique`) and inserted the single `ensureIdentityUnique` step *after* `assignHousehold`, so the `householdId` component of the key is already populated when the check runs.\n\n**Response** \u2014 added a read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`; MapStruct auto-maps it from the entity getter, so creates and GETs now return `identityKey`.\n\n**Removed** the three old `EnsureOwner*Unique` classes, three `Duplicate*Exception`/handler pairs, and their escalation YAMLs; fixed the stale `{@link}` in `AssignHouseholdId`.\n\n## Behaviour change (as specified)\nBecause telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have distinct keys and are both allowed. I updated the one existing test that asserted the old household-only rejection (`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`): same-household + different-telephone is renamed `createOwnerAllowsSameHouseholdWithDifferentTelephone` and now expects `201 Created`. The telephone-duplicate and acknowledged-shared-household tests still pass unchanged, since an exact full-key collision (same telephone) is still a 409.\n\nFull suite: **261 passed, 0 failures**.",
